    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33335" root="فر" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُرَافِرٌ</span></b>  A horse <i>that moves about,</i> or <i>agitates, the
bit in his mouth,</i> (M, O, K, TA,) to which Z adds,
<i>in order that he may disengage it</i> [<i>therefrom,</i> or]
<i>from his head.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْرَقُ</span> [<i>Rough,
ungentle,</i> &amp;c.]; (M, O, K;) applied to a man.
(O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرْفَارٌ</span>, in two places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُرَارٌ</span>, likewise in two places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُرْفُورٌ</span>, also in
two places.

